{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For the east side, eastward.</b> The face of the east; קֶדֶם is a term of 'front,' אָחוֹר is a term of 'back.' Therefore the east is called קֶדֶם because it is the front, and the west is called אָחוֹר, as you say ״הַיָּם הָאַחֲרוֹן״ (Deuteronomy 11:24, Deut. 34:2) — יַמָּא מַעַרְבָא." "<b>Fifty cubits.</b> Those fifty cubits were not all enclosed with hangings, because the entrance was there — but fifteen cubits of hangings for the shoulder of the entrance on this side, and likewise for the second shoulder. The width of the opening of the entrance between them remained twenty cubits. And this is what is said ״וּלְשַׁעַר הֶחָצֵר מָסָךְ כְּעֶשְׂרִים אַמָּה״ — a curtain-screen for the entrance, twenty cubits long, equal to the width of the entrance."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:57.719446498Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}